{"title":"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca8e1ed0a0d34754cdd985dfc1d6683a066da7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> are all equilateral. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79acca1cedca0d43e9d183383ef794ad7932baa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, what is the perimeter of figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9019ab2a2a7f9aa8571013ba36766862a73df7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFG$\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee31377617710d02efbfe48eb576a433c3499ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,EE,F,G; A = (4,0); B = (0,0); C = (2,2*sqrt(3)); D = (3,sqrt(3)); EE = (5,sqrt(3)); F = (5.5,sqrt(3)/2); G = (4.5,sqrt(3)/2); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--EE--A); draw(EE--F--G); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,EE,NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,SE);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/5070c47f4a437332203f9bddb296883ee3dbf0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 12\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ 13\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ 15\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ 18\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The large triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The medium triangle has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The small triangle has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> segment sizes, and all segments depicted are one of these lengths.\n</p><p>Starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and going clockwise, the perimeter is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480855cec6d59dbd362b2a7cf14d59e1deff6ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BC + CD + DE + EF + FG + GA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"335\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4ac1f244c6f362e2b6187d00665e6fc272b6acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 4 + 2 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9019ab2a2a7f9aa8571013ba36766862a73df7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFG$\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> is the perimeter of the three triangles, minus segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, which are on the interior of the figure.  Because each of these segments is on two triangles, each segment must be subtracted two times.\n</p><p>As in solution 1, the sides of the triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d298e3514275f0da1d9172884221606e4afd35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the perimeters of the triangles are thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/2373340ec5f418124872e64378482819025e2c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12, 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The perimeter of the three triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533f8e115811b3ea28f54b7c89e3910285003baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 6 + 3 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />.  Subtracting the two segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> two times, the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9019ab2a2a7f9aa8571013ba36766862a73df7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFG$\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/11602f93380b98ebd0c911bf5aa79a9ba16fb1ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 - 2 - 1 - 2 - 1 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"185\" height=\"13\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, remove segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Notice that segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can fit into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. This means we only need to account for the perimeters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca8e1ed0a0d34754cdd985dfc1d6683a066da7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, whose perimeters are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Adding these perimeters gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c37d0edddfbbff5082485dc36fb5c65810eed88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+3=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, or answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n~Electric_Cheetah_88\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 8\">2000 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017193700\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 299/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8298/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.854      1 -total\n 56.51%    7.829      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 41.14%    5.699      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9863:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017193700 and revision id 268151. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}